    { "ref": "TP206", "signal": "+LO/HI I", "rail": "CONTROL", "kind": "wire-loop",
      "refPoint": "TP203", "nominal": 2.65, "tolerance": 0.65, "unit": "V",
      "condition": "Power on, standby (control line released, A12-A16 out)",
      "inferred": true,
      "source": "Measured 2.65 V on a bench unit with A12-A16 removed, and bounded by Figure 7-22 sheet 2 zone A7. NOT §5-23 step 4: that gives +12 V +/-4 V for TP205/207/208 only, and this net cannot reach it.",
      "note": "Not a Z201 control line like TP205/207/208, despite tapping the same pull-up bus. R251 (4.7 K to +5LHR) swamps Z201's 100 K, and the level is that pull-up loaded by Q217's own base current -- which is why it rests near 2.6 V and not at 5 V. VR245 clamps the net at 3.3 V, so +12 V is not reachable here at all. Limits: 3.3 V is the clamp, 2.0 V is the same node with a low-gain Q217. Around 0 V means the line is being held low or R251 has gone open; around 5 V means Q217's base is open and K201 will never pull in. Drives Q217, which switches relay K201 to select the current limit for both +/-PA supplies.",
      "onFail": [ "R251", "VR245", "Q217", "Z201" ] }
